+A holomorphic compatible cone entirely inside an actual centre-preimage divisor can pull its nonzero invertible ideal back to the zero ideal. Thus the weak ideal-invertibility blowup universal property alone does NOT prove the unrestricted holomorphic Cartesian square for arbitrary cones. Genuine local product blowup charts, their actual atlas transitions and genuine choice comparison are still needed to produce smoothness of the actual lifted map and the unrestricted Cartesian universal property. General higher-invariant functoriality, noncompact general termination, old-driver identification, unrelated ideal admissibility, whole G3/G8 and formal/native/publication remain OPEN. 
